<title>FINLAND: Finnair Oct passenger load factor falls.</title>
<headline>Finnair Oct passenger load factor falls.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national airline Finnair Oy said in a statement on Friday its passenger load factor fell 2.3 percentage points year-on-year in October to 65.1 percent.  </p>
<p>Finnair gave the following statistics:</p>
<p>					Oct 1996   Sept 1996   Yr/yr(pct)</p>
<p> Passengers (thousand)	     547	   547	 +3.2</p>
<p> RPK (million)			 881	   849	 -3.7</p>
<p> RTK (million)			 102	    98	 +2.3</p>
<p> Cargo and mail (thousand kg)  5,195	 5,418	 +3.1</p>
<p> Passenger load factor (pct)    65.1	  68.9	 -2.3 pts</p>
<p>October 1996 totals broken down by flight type:</p>
<p>			Passengers   RPK	 RTK	    Cargo</p>
<p>			thousand   million    million     thousand kg</p>
<p> International	 275	 580	  75	    4,568</p>
<p> Domestic		195	  81	   7		519</p>
<p> Charter		  77	 220	  20		109</p>
<p>Load factor (percent) by flight type:</p>
<p>				  Oct 1996  Sept 1996  Yr/yr (pct pts)</p>
<p> International		  62.7	 65.6	  -2.7</p>
<p> Domestic			 54.3	 57.2	  +1.6</p>
<p>Finnair's financial year runs from April 1 to March 31.</p>
<p>In April-October, Finnair's passenger load factor was 0.7 percentage points down year-on-year at 69.3 percent. Passengers carried were up 5.5 percent at 3.77 million, but revenue passenger km was only 0.2 percent higher at 6.34 million.</p>
<p>RPK - revenue passenger km (revenue passengers carried multiplied by km flown)</p>
<p>RTK - revenue tonne km (tonnage of revenue load carried -- passengers, cargo and mail -- multiplied by km flown.</p>
<p>Passenger load factor - RPK as a percentage of available seat km</p>
<p>Finnair does not give a cargo load factor.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 235</p>
</text>
